# Palette provenance

Six themes are Adea-authored: the composed Adea Light and Dark defaults, and the Slate
and High Contrast light/dark variants. The other twenty-five themes reproduce
third-party palettes. This section records the sources, terms, and where those values
came from. The per-theme machine-readable form is on each catalogue entry's
`provenance` field, and `tests/provenance.test.ts` asserts the published source values.

## The chain of custody

The colour values in `palettes/` were not typed in by hand, and they are not read
from any package at runtime. They were produced once, by
`scripts/vendor-palettes.ts`, which reproduces the Base24 scheme for each theme from
one pinned revision of:

- **oklch-terminal-themes** — https://github.com/williamzujkowski/oklch-terminal-themes
  — revision `9e800e7fe760081d4c10317498038ed4227341d6` — MIT.
  This is the bootstrap dataset. Its Base24 schemes are, in turn, derived from the
  terminal ports published in:
- **iTerm2-Color-Schemes** — https://github.com/mbadolato/iTerm2-Color-Schemes — MIT.

`oklch-terminal-themes` is a build-time input only. It is not a dependency of this
package, in either `dependencies` or `devDependencies`, and nothing here reads it at
run time. What it contributed is a starting set of values, which was then checked
against each palette's own project before being committed.

