# Contrast repairs

Some themes in this catalogue do not ship the exact colour a palette specifies for
every role, because the palette's own value fails a contrast floor on the palette's
own background. Solarized Light's body text is the clearest case: `#657b83` on
`#fdf6e3` measures 4.28:1, below the WCAG AA floor of 4.5:1.

Where that happens, the value's **lightness** is moved by the smallest amount that
clears the floor, and nothing else is changed — OKLCH makes that a single-axis edit
that preserves hue and chroma exactly, and `tests/provenance.test.ts` asserts the hue
is unmoved. In the rare case where lightness alone cannot reach the floor, the colour
is blended toward the palette's own foreground, which is recorded on the entry and
reported on every build. No colour is ever invented: every value in the catalogue is
a value from the palette it is attributed to, viewed at a different brightness.

